## PART F: FURTHER EXTENSIONS & FUTURE WORK

### F.1 What the Agent Could Work On Next

| Extension | Description |
|---|---|
| **Sentiment tracking** | Deploy the sentiment scrape spec (separate file) to monitor public reaction to the 1 Dec policy |
| **Enforcement simulation** | Model inspection coverage: 12 inspectors × 40,000 sites = what % compliance? |
| **Climate projection overlay** | Run the policy thresholds against IPCC SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5 scenarios for Singapore 2035/2050 |
| **Migrant worker voice** | Partner with TWC2 or Migrant Workers' Centre to gather ground-truth data (ethical approval required) |
| **Cost-benefit analysis** | Quantify: cost of compliance vs. cost of heat-illness hospitalisations + workers' comp claims |
| **Regulatory impact statement** | Draft a formal RIS for the policy, as required under Singapore's regulatory process |
| **Parliamentary briefing** | Produce a 2-page brief for MPs ahead of a WSH Act amendment debate |
| **International benchmarking report** | Full comparison: SG vs CA vs Qatar vs AU vs EU — who has the strongest standard? |
| **Gig-economy extension** | Analyse whether delivery riders (Grab, Foodpanda, Deliveroo) are covered or excluded |
| **Insurance linkage** | Model whether WSH insurance premiums could be indexed to heat-compliance scores |

### F.2 Countries to Watch (Emerging / Pending)

| Country | Status | Why It Matters |
|---|---|---|
| USA (Federal OSHA) | ANPRM stalled since 2021 | If enacted, becomes global benchmark |
| India | Heat Action Plans advisory | 200M+ outdoor workers; no binding law |
| EU | Framework Directive generic | If EU adds specific heat threshold, affects all 27 members |
| UK | No specific heat law | Post-Brexit divergence from EU possible |
| Brazil | NR-15 (heat exposure limits) | Relevant for tropical comparison |
| South Africa | OHS Act general duty | African comparator |
| Philippines | DOLE guidelines | ASEAN comparator |
| Vietnam | Labour Code heat provisions | ASEAN comparator |
| Indonesia | Manpower Law general welfare | ASEAN comparator |
| Nigeria | No specific heat law | High-vulnerability, zero-protection case |

